        <item>
            <title>1.5.13</title>
            <pubDate>Sat, 01 Aug 2026 22:29:14 +0900</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>45</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.5.13</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h3>Added</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Per-folder view mode, like Windows Explorer.</b> Each folder now remembers the view you chose for it — Extra Large/Large/Medium/Small Icons, List, or Details — and restores it every time you return, across tabs, navigation routes, and app restarts. Folders you haven't customized default to Details. Subfolders without their own setting inherit the view of the nearest customized parent folder (without saving it), so a photo library set to Large Icons browses in Large Icons all the way down; explicitly choosing a view in a subfolder — including Details — pins it. Stored settings are bounded (least-recently-used, 1,000 folders) and live in app preferences — nothing is written into your folders.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Fixed</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Rare crash in the address-bar suggestion dropdown.</b> Dismissing the typed-history dropdown while the list was still updating could crash the app (index out of range during a deferred layout pass).</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
